      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/4491bb/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-08-21T09:48:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Are we completely sure about this? I'm taking your words on it, and I believe you. I just couldn't find a rule to back you guys up. The companions have a rule specifically on their rules page that says they get lifted off when the power cards is removed. Citizen Dawn's power card that puts out a Citizen has rules printed on it that tells you if it leaves play the targets leave play too. There are no rules printed on the Impaling Structure's power card that specify that if it leaves play so do the structures. I also couldn't find a rule for them in the rulebook to make them do that. I believe you guys because I like how that works and want it to work that way but I'm wondering if you guys have rules that I might be missing to back it up. It's just odd to me that on other cards, and in other rules sections, it had to specify that the markers get removed, but here it doesn't specify at all. However, I don't know how the impaling structures would continue to generate hazzard spaces without their power card defining them.</p>",
